{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeuoicWH6fQNSitToxwwM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n\n- Order entity at `Order.kt:11-16` — currently has no status field\n- OrderController at `OrderController.kt:15-47` — has create, getById, list; no cancel endpoint\n- OrderRepository at `OrderRepository.kt:11-27` — in-memory ConcurrentHashMap, basic CRUD\n- Shipment already has status enum at `Shipment.kt:23-27` with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController at `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — creates shipments with CREATED status, does not validate order state\n- ShipmentRepository at `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — in-memory store, no method to find by orderId\n- Exception handling at `ApiExceptions.kt:11-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) exist\n- Error codes at `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n- Exceptions thrown in controllers are caught by GlobalExceptionHandler and converted to ApiError response envelope\n- All error responses use the envelope structure: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"CODE\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n- Tests use MockMvc with @SpringBootTest, assert both status and error body structure\n- Controllers return ResponseEntity with appropriate HTTP status codes\n- Shipment already demonstrates status management pattern with enum\n- In-memory repositories use ConcurrentHashMap with simple find methods\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `Order.kt` — must add status field (required for new feature)\n2. `OrderController.kt` — must add cancel endpoint (required for feature)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add method to find shipments by orderId (required to query shipments during cancel)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — must validate order status before creating shipment (required to prevent shipments for cancelled orders)\n5. `ApiError.kt` — may need new error codes for order-state-related failures\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for cancel endpoint\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — may need tests for shipment creation rejection\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Adding status to Order changes the data contract; need to ensure new orders default to ACTIVE\n- All-or-nothing cancel semantics requires atomic check-then-update across orders and shipments\n- Shipment repository needs efficient lookup by orderId to cancel all shipments\n- Test isolation depends on proper cleanup between tests\n\n**Open questions:** None — ticket is explicit on all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class; add OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint. Logic:\n   - Get order by id → 404 if not found\n   - If already CANCELLED → return it as-is (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED → throw ConflictException 409, change nothing (checked before any update)\n   - Otherwise → mark order as CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, return updated order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order. Used during cancel to check for CONFIRMED shipments and cancel CREATED ones.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — In create endpoint, after validating shipment doesn't exist, validate that the order exists AND is not CANCELLED. If order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException 409. If order doesn't exist, current behavior (silently accept) is unchanged per ticket requirement \"Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current behaviour.\"\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add two new error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for when creating shipment on cancelled order), `CANNOT_CANCEL_ORDER_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (for when order has CONFIRMED shipment).\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests covering:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns it with status CANCELLED\n   - Cancelling already CANCELLED order succeeds unchanged\n   - Cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409, changes nothing\n   - Cancelling non-existent order returns 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test for creating shipment on cancelled order returns 409.\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered creating a separate service/business logic layer to handle the cancel logic (similar to BE-003 which likely adds a confirm endpoint). However, the codebase shows controllers calling repositories directly without an intermediate service layer, so adding a service layer would be an unrelated refactoring. Staying consistent with existing patterns, cancel logic goes in the controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n**Case 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with only CREATED shipments**\n- Read: Order from repo → must exist, must be ACTIVE\n- Write: Order status → CANCELLED; all shipments with status CREATED → CANCELLED\n- Caller receives: Order with status=CANCELLED, 200 OK\n- Mechanism: Direct repository save\n\n**Case 2: Cancel already CANCELLED order**\n- Read: Order from repo → must exist\n- Write: None (idempotent)\n- Caller receives: Order with status=CANCELLED, 200 OK\n- Mechanism: Return existing order\n\n**Case 3: Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment**\n- Read: Order from repo → must exist; all shipments for order\n- Write: None (all-or-nothing)\n- Caller receives: 409 ConflictException with error code CANNOT_CANCEL_ORDER_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\n- Mechanism: Check before any write; exception is caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n**Case 4: Cancel non-existent order**\n- Read: Order from repo → null\n- Write: None\n- Caller receives: 404 ResourceNotFoundException with error code ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- Mechanism: findById returns null, throw before any write\n\n**Case 5: Create shipment for CANCELLED order**\n- Read: Shipment doesn't exist (check); Order exists and is CANCELLED (check)\n- Write: None\n- Caller receives: 409 ConflictException with error code ORDER_CANCELLED\n- Mechanism: Check during create validation\n\n**Case 6: Create shipment for non-existent order** (unchanged per ticket)\n- Read: Shipment doesn't exist (check); Order not checked\n- Write: Shipment with status CREATED\n- Caller receives: 201 Created with Shipment\n- Mechanism: No change to current behavior\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. OrderControllerTest — new tests for cancel endpoint\n   - Test: Cancel active order → status 200, order.status = CANCELLED\n   - Test: Cancel already cancelled order → status 200, unchanged\n   - Test: Cancel with confirmed shipment → status 409, error code CANNOT_CANCEL_ORDER_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, order unchanged\n   - Test: Cancel unknown order → status 404, error code ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - Test: Verify CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n\n2. ShipmentControllerTest — new test for rejection\n   - Test: Create shipment on cancelled order → status 409, error code ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n3. All existing tests must pass unchanged (backward compatibility).\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start by modifying Order.kt to add the status field:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":603,"cache_read_input_tokens":22367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":603},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23888851-827d-4eb1-8fed-a470c48c5fca","uuid":"3a95f887-7125-472a-864a-28337ebea8fe","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:04:57.943Z","request_id":"req_011Ceuoibqqi5unFjsqGCBvi"}
